From: PS4 port
Subject: [PATCH] orbis: the recompiler targets the SysV ABI

Same cause as 0001 - a C++ TU here has no platform macro, because this SDK's libc++ undefines
__FreeBSD__ on purpose - and the same shape of consequence: eleven `#error Unknown ABI.` and
every register name the recompiler defines behind that branch (RARG1, RCPUPTR, RMEMBASEPTR,
RRETURN, FUNCTION_CALL_SHADOW_SPACE) reported as undeclared identifiers.

This one is not a guess about what the console prefers. The target triple is
x86_64-pc-freebsd12-elf and everything in this port is built for it, so the calling convention IS
System V - the same arm __FreeBSD__ already selects two lines up.

diff --git a/src/core/cpu_recompiler_types.h b/src/core/cpu_recompiler_types.h
index ab2431a..8f5fd4a 100644
--- a/src/core/cpu_recompiler_types.h
+++ b/src/core/cpu_recompiler_types.h
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ constexpr uint32_t CODE_STORAGE_ALIGNMENT = 4096;
 // ABI selection
 #if defined(_WIN32)
 #define ABI_WIN64 1
-#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__HAIKU__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__HAIKU__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__ORBIS__)
 #define ABI_SYSV 1
 #else
 #error Unknown ABI.
